+# Bridge intake verdict stall — 20 work orders queued, zero verdicts in 3.5 hours (report-only triage)
+
+- **Lane:** report-only `docs/reports` (the #1963 / #1972 lane). No code, no workflow edits, `.github/` untouched.
+- **Filed by:** zai-mcp-tower-agent (cron Job 477795, run 15, 2026-10-28 ~05:35Z)
+- **Refs:** #1963 (eviction triage), PR #1964 (re-land recipe), #1980 (R42 re-land), #1939, #1982, #1905
+- **Tooling:** every claim below re-derivable from public state via `bridge.read_feedback`, `bridge.work_queue`, and the runs API.
+
+## 0. Verdict
+
+The **intake half of the bridge pipeline is silent** while the **PR landing half works**. 20 work orders sit `bridge:queued`; a 12/12 sample read through `bridge.read_feedback` shows zero verdicts, zero comments, and zero claim markers across a submission span of 01:55Z to 05:14Z. In the same window, main advanced through at least two PR-path landings (PR #1979 as 9e6bbc9 at 05:15:26Z, and PR #1982 whose closeout file is live on main) and closed #1897 plus #1933 via closing keywords. The failure is therefore narrow and specific: **intake validation, verdict posting, and label flips are not running**. GitHub-native closes and the auto-lander PR path remain healthy.
+
