+
+## 3. Root cause hypotheses (ranked)
+
+- **H1 — Intake worker desync from the eviction.** Intake evaluation may anchor on head SHAs; the force-push rollback to d75596d could fail-close every queued evaluation against a tip it cannot reconcile. Best fit for timing: the stall begins inside the eviction window.
+- **H2 — Intake worker outage, independent of the eviction** (process down, scheduled run not firing). Cannot be distinguished from H1 without admin-side logs.
+- **H3 — Verdict posting broken while private-repo landing continues.** If gated PRs exist in the private repo for these 20 items, work is being processed but results are never posted back. Distinguishable by R2 below.
+
+## 4. Impact
+
+- **Submitter blindness.** No APPLIED/REJECTED signal for the whole window; the one-way feedback blindness that `bridge.read_feedback` was built to close (#621) is back in effect for every submitter active since 01:55Z.
+- **Duplicate hazard.** Agents seeing a silent queue re-file the same work — the exact #1692 audit class, where one submission produced duplicate orders minutes apart.
+- **Distorted metrics.** `bridge.work_queue` reports 20 pending regardless of actual private-repo progress; capacity decisions made from it are unsound while the stall lasts.
+- **Loop dispatch idles.** Mirror issues #1897 and #1933 are closed, but their resolution vehicles (#1905, #1939 triage docs) sit queued with no visible verdict, so the next failure cycle has no confirmed landing lane for triage work.
+- **Compounding.** The auto-close-on-merge gap flagged at run 14 (Telegram msg 1851: #1891, #1914, #1931 still open after their PRs merged) degrades lifecycle signals at the tail; this stall degrades them at the head. Together they make the board unreadable from the agent side.
+
+## 5. Admin recipes
+
+- **R1 —** Pull intake worker logs from 04:00Z onward; restart if dead. A crash trace referencing the evicted SHAs d9d9385 or 7f8d8df confirms H1.
+- **R2 —** Check the private-repo gate PR queue for items #1899 through #1980. Gated PRs present means H3 (backfill verdicts only); absent means H1/H2 (restart, then re-run intake).
+- **R3 —** Backfill verdicts on all 20 queued items after recovery; `bridge.read_feedback` makes the backfill machine-readable for every submitter.
+- **R4 —** Watchdog mirror: alert when the oldest `bridge:queued` item exceeds about 45 minutes with zero verdict comments. Against today's data it would have fired near 02:40Z — hours before any human noticed.
+- **R5 —** Decouple verdict posting from landing: post an ACK verdict at intake validation time and follow with landing status as a second event. This removes the blindness class even during landing outages.
+- **R6 —** Standing, 5th notice: PR #1810 rescue — recipe live in CONTRIBUTING §11 since run 11.
+- **R7 —** Standing: auto-close-on-merge for work-order issues (flagged run 14).
+
+## 6. Scope guard
+
+Report-only: one new file under `docs/reports/`; no code paths, no `.github/` paths, no workflow edits, no other agent's branch touched. This report intentionally adds itself to the stalled queue: it is simultaneously the incident record for the R3 backfill and a live probe — the moment intake posts a verdict on it, recovery is confirmed.
